limitations.en:
- **Web platform only**;
- The plugin replaces the renderer for the "Completed in …" row, which is how the avatar fits in the left gutter — **refresh once after disabling or uninstalling it**, otherwise that row shows "unknown surface event: turn-process";
- The avatar appears only after a turn finishes; streaming turns have none (that would require replacing the whole answer renderer);
- Conflicts with other plugins that also replace `turn-process`;
- Read-aloud is split by sentence; a failed sentence is skipped;
- The service launcher's host code loads at DSH startup, so **restart DSH after upgrading the plugin**;
- That feature **runs local programs with the command you type** — only point it at your own service; the route is same-origin on your machine and has no extra auth, so don't expose DSH to the internet;
- In the English UI the preview reads an English sentence; a Chinese-trained voice will carry an accent — that is the model, not the plugin.

- **DSH versions**: `0.2.0-rc.2` / `0.2.1-rc.2`; depends on the base bundle's `sessionProjections`, `settings` and `configEditor` — missing ones degrade gracefully: no projections → sidebar marker / progress card unavailable; no settings → read-only config;
- **Node.js >= 22.19.0** (the client uses React 18+ `useSyncExternalStore`);
- **Creation happens only on the first step of a Session's first turn** and only for top-level Sessions whose recorded creation source is `startup`; resume / clear / compaction / subagents / taskboard sessions / matching presets / disable marker / `enabled: false` / existing record / placement=local never create one. A blank Session that is opened and never used creates nothing, so a placement choice made in it is read at send time and cannot lag one Session behind;
- **No new Workspace**: sessions stay in their original workspace; only the cwd changes;
- **No naming, no branch** (detached by default); `mode: branch` is opt-in; the plugin never merges, pushes or deletes user branches;
- **Non-Git workspaces**: the selector is hidden and nothing is created;
- **Read-only sandbox / workspace-write boundary / no commit / limit**: structured errors that never block the session;
- concurrent creation in one repository is serialized by `createKeyedMutex`; any exception inside the `agent/pre-step` listener is swallowed and warned about, so the plugin can never prevent a session from starting or block the first message;
- projection events enter the session log (~4 per new session), the cost of zero polling; an ephemeral channel could replace them later (out of scope for this release);
- **known limitation**: cleaning a non-live session's checkout from the settings page leaves its sidebar marker until that session's next consistency repair (reopening the session or its first step; see 2.4);
- **seat choice (by design, not a limitation)**: the placement pill registers in the official `conversation.hero.options` list seat, **not** the single-value `conversation.hero.workspace` seat owned by the shipped WorkspacePicker (that seat is `kind: "single"` with `replaceRisk: "shadows-shipped-ui"`), so the shipped workspace switcher is **never shadowed**; the sidebar marker uses the official ambient-marker seat `sidebar.session.row.leading`, not the hover-only row action strip;
- the sidebar marker is only a marker: not clickable, no hover card, no navigation;
- the "don't use a worktree" rollback feature is **explicitly out of scope**; the progress card's "Cancel" only hides the card.

- **The cost of force-cleaning**: overriding `worktree-in-use` makes the **other** live session lose its current working directory (its cwd points at a deleted checkout) and throws away any uncommitted changes in it; cleaning your own session's checkout is not refused, its cwd is moved back to the original workspace.
- **Restored checkouts are not managed by the plugin**: they are not written to sidecar records and are not bound to a session, so remove them manually with `git worktree remove`; snapshots only hold the pre-delete committed HEAD.
- **Snapshots only contain committed content**: the ref points at the pre-delete `HEAD`, so uncommitted changes are not in it; a restored checkout is not bound to the original session either.
- **Archive cleanup is a lazy sweep**: `cleanupOnArchive` is not immediate; it only runs at the moments listed in 6.3, and skips checkouts still used by a live session.

Out of scope: cloud / Codex Web integration / multiple placements; automatic merge, PRs, environment installation; remembering placement per session (instead of per workspace); switching an existing session into a worktree mid-conversation.

- Depends on the sidebar's internal markup and on `SessionSummary.parentSessionId` (a private contract); a redesign can break it, in which case it silently stops;
- Collapse state is in memory and resets on reload;
- Row order is corrected in the render layer; the `MutationObserver` re-corrects if the host re-sorts;
- Only mounted (visible) rows are handled.

For loading placeholders followed by “No matching sessions” after opening Cost,
see [non-destructive sidebar search recovery](docs/session-sidebar-recovery.md).
Check and clear the host search before changing stored data.

- Official-page parsing depends on the current page structure; after a redesign, “Sync prices from official docs” fails — edit the price table manually as a fallback;
- The session badge's fallback estimate (used when ledger data is unavailable) prices all of a session's calls at the tier of the *current* moment, including plan-type sessions: a session spanning peak and off-peak hours gets its off-peak portion overestimated during peak hours; exact figures come from the ledger (which bills each call at its own initiation moment);
- Price sync overwrites the same-named models listed on the official page; custom model entries are unaffected;
- Balance lookup needs network access to api.deepseek.com and a valid API key; **the API key is only ever sent to the official domain** (if baseURL points at a non-official host, balance queries refuse to run — model requests are unaffected);
- The OpenCode Go quota endpoint is the official opencode.ai endpoint (community-documented); if its response shape changes, the Settings page shows an error and the display can be turned off in Display settings;
- The per-1% quota / full-window figures in Token Plan stats are estimates: vendors only report percentages with ones-digit quantization (a displayed 1% may really be 0.5%–1.5%), so the plugin derives them from end-to-end deltas over continuous sample segments to suppress quantization noise (segments spanning <5 percentage points are tagged "low reading precision"; samples older than 7 days fall back to live ratio; window edges align to whole hours). Server percentages cover ALL usage of the account — consumption of the same key on other machines/CLIs is not in the local ledger, so low estimates are expected; treat them as cross-plan comparisons only;
- Plan/API classification is inferred from channel and config; mixed subscription/PAYG usage of one vendor (e.g. Kimi) can be overridden per provider:model in settings.
- A restart of `dsh web` is required after installing/updating the plugin.

limitations.zh:
打开费用设置后若侧栏出现加载占位条与「No matching sessions」，请先查看
[无损侧栏搜索恢复说明](docs/session-sidebar-recovery.md)，检查宿主搜索内容，
不要删除会话、账本或浏览器存储。

- 历史按模型回填依赖宿主会话日志仍在盘:日志已被清理的早期调用无法逐模型重建,只能以「未分模型」残差行计入当日合计;
